← [38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Approach [39m[49m ☐ Tooling  ✔ Submit  →

[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach to the rule model?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mB: rules-as-functions map (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mForms declare {field: [rule, ...]}; rules are (value, allData) => error|null closures from factories. ~30-line [39m
     [38;5;246mengine. Custom and cross-field rules need no registry.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m A: predicate helpers only
     [38;5;246mJust shared isNonEmpty/isEmail/hasMinLength helpers; each form writes its own validate function. Smallest, but [39m
     [38;5;246mleaves the per-form collect-errors boilerplate duplicated.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: serializable descriptor schema
     [38;5;246mRules as JSON data interpreted via a rule registry. Enables sharing schemas with a backend later, at the cost of [39m
     [38;5;246mnotably more machinery.[39m
